<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reggio Emilia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Reggio nell'Emilia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reggio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilia">Emilia</a> is a city in Emilia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-aemilia">Via Emilia</a> between Parma and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as Regium Lepidi. A medieval commune, it passed to the Este in 1409 and formed part of the Duchy of Modena and Reggio until 1859. The Italian tricolour flag was adopted there by the Cispadane Republic in 1797.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia.jpg" alt="Reggio Emilia" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paolo Picciati · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reggio_emilia_panorama_e_Ghiara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
